@title PCSA00015 front end - title screen and GAME MODE
@game  PCSA00015
# (no cadence shots - judge this title through `vitaslop-desktop --headless`)

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
# Boots the title and drives its TOUCH front end:
#
#   loading -> attract demo -> PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START -> GAME MODE (4 tiles)
#
# >>> RETIMED 2026-08-17d. THE OLD FRAME NUMBERS WERE FIVE TIMES TOO LATE.
# The committed version pressed its first button at f28000, which was right when
# it was authored and is not right now: on the derived guest clock the loading
# screen finishes about f5040 and the attract demo is running by f5100, so every
# cue fired long after the screen it was aimed at and the run never left the
# attract loop. Do not scale these numbers by hand if the clock moves again -
# re-measure with `VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_EVERY` and look at the shots.
#
# HOW THESE FRAMES WERE MEASURED (repeat this, do not guess):
#   VITASLOP_GXP_LIVE=1 VITASLOP_GXP_ALLOW_FIXED_FUNCTION=1 \
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_FRAMES=9200 VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_EVERY=200 \
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_FROM=5200 VITASLOP_LOG=error \
#   vitaslop-desktop --game <wipeout>/extracted --recipe <this> --headless <dir>
# `VITASLOP_GXP_ALLOW_FIXED_FUNCTION=1` is for FINDING FRAMES ONLY - one draw on
# the loading path still blocks on USSE group 0x1d, and without it a periodic
# shot that lands on that frame kills the run. Take the judged shot WITHOUT it.
#
# >>> THE SCREEN THIS RECIPE EXISTS FOR IS THE TITLE SCREEN AT ~f5600.
# White frame, the hex lattice, the logo, PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START and the
# copyright line. That lattice is the over-embossed one the user has reported:
# see `working-area/agent-notes.md` for what is measured about it.
#
# TOUCH COORDINATES are in PANEL coordinates, which are screen*2.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
# No input while it loads. Loading reaches 99% by about f5035 and the attract
# demo takes over immediately after.

5150: cross
5170:
# Any button during the attract demo brings up the title screen: WIPEOUT 2048
# over the hex lattice, PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START. It is up from about f5200.

5450: cross
5470:
# >>> THE TITLE SCREEN WANTS A BUTTON, NOT A TOUCH, AND THAT IS WHAT THE OLD
# RECIPE GOT WRONG. It had `touch=472,524` here - the SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN
# tile's coordinates, aimed at a GAME MODE screen that was not up yet - so the
# tap fell on PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START, which ignores it, and the run sat on
# the title screen for the rest of its length. The screen is measurably still
# there at f6400 under the old cue and gone by f5700 under this one.
# GAME MODE (four tiles) is up by about f5750.

5750: touch=472,524
5790:
# The SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN tile (screen 236,262). The two greyed tiles are
# ONLINE CAMPAIGN and CROSS-PLAY - this build is signed out, so they are
# correctly unavailable. The campaign INTRO ("It's the year 2048...") is up by
# about f6000 and waits on its confirm button.

6200: touch=1764,960
6240:
# The confirm tick, bottom right (screen 882,480). Past it is the CAMPAIGN MAP:
# the A.G.R.C 2048 hex chain, with the first event node captioned TOUCH TO START
# and every later node still locked. It is up by about f6700.

7000: touch=1016,570
7040:
# That first node (screen 508,285).
